      "message": "To fully avoid interleaved loads and prevent reading `input.alpha` twice, consider moving all the local variable loads above the `push_back` call. A function call like `push_back` could potentially act as a compiler barrier and interfere with the optimal loads you are trying to achieve here.\n\n```cpp\nconst uint8_t blue \u003d input.blue;\nconst uint8_t green \u003d input.green;\nconst uint8_t red \u003d input.red;\nconst uint8_t alpha \u003d input.alpha;\njpx_inline_data_.data.push_back(alpha);\n\n// Compiler can\u0027t conclude src/dest don\u0027t overlap.\n// ...\n```",
